"Postoperative prognosis depends on the preoperative PSA and the prostatectomy findings. Extraprostatic extension is documented. Positive surgical margins is documented. Seminal vesicle invasion is documented. Lymphovascular invasion is reported absent. Postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory are needed to refine this prognosis; a future recurrence date cannot be established from surgical risk factors alone. The fixed estimated horizon is 34.46 months. This is a predicted recurrence horizon, not evidence of observed recurrence. The sensitivity range is 27.57–41.35 months; its coverage has not been validated."
